Z||000000||Jackalrr||12-22-2000||02:09 PM||||I noticed that my oil was leaking. It has been aprox. 2,800 miles since my last change. I cannot see exactly where the oil is coming from. The oil filter was loose but the problem has continued even after tightening. Could this be a gasket somewhere?<P>BTW: it is an 85 GT<P>Thanks,<BR>-Charlie<BR>------<BR>jackalrr@cinci.rr.com||||reg||5
Z||000001||2xsess||12-22-2000||02:39 PM||||can you see any oil deposits anywhere?<P>It could be the distributor o-ring or a number of other seals.<BR>You have to look and see if you can find any evidence of the leak.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||5
Z||000002||Oreif||12-22-2000||02:48 PM||||You could buy some spray-on grease remover, (I think it's called "Gunk") and spray the bottom, hose it off and drive it. Upon returning you should be able to trace the leak. Shine a flash light at the base of the distributor and look just below ths hold down clamp. If you see fresh oil it's the O-ring. To stop all my leaks I had to replace O-ring and oil pan gasket. (Both were leaking when I bought the car)<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-22-2000).]||||reg||1
